{
	"$comment": "Cross-repository conformance spec for the two PIE i18n engines: pie-players' players-shared/src/i18n and pie-elements-ng's @pie-element/shared-i18n, which ports it and shares semantics but no code. Each repository runs this file against its own engine. Keep the two copies byte-identical: pie-players packages/players-shared/tests/i18n-conformance-fixtures.json and pie-elements-ng packages/shared/i18n/tests/i18n-conformance-fixtures.json. A case that only one engine passes is drift, and the fix goes to the engine, not the fixture. Locale tags are full where CLDR defaults differ by region: bare `ar` formats Latin digits and `ar-SA` Arabic-Indic, which is CLDR, not an engine.",
	"lookupSequence": [
		{ "tag": "nl-BE", "expected": ["nl-be", "nl"] },
